    "language": "[0][1]All right. So just do the same thing again? Yeah, do the same thing again and don't forget, like I think you're doing a great job with this, but, like have some variance in it, like- Yeah. ... turn different directions. Okay. And also, one more thing is, when you say \"you\" in the system, like \"you\" is supposed to be like you actually. Like don't say like your teammate if you're referring to your teammate. That's- Oh, okay. I see. Okay. All right. So otherwise you'll be confusing the defender. All right. So, I'm gonna start off by checking closer to the teammate so that the defender isn't as close to me. [2]After I check closer, I see that the defender is on my right, so I'm gonna check to the left and get closer to, to the teammate so I can turn. [3][4]I see that the pass comes down the middle, so I'm not gonna be able to turn around, so I'm gonna receive the ball and try to pass it back to you. [5][6]As I receive the ball, I see the defender is right, is, is very close to me, so I'm gonna pass it back. [7]You[8] should be able to do that. Okay.[9]",
